---
import FrameworkLayout from '../../layouts/FrameworkLayout.astro';

const sections = ['Overview', 'Core Principles', 'Creating Blue Oceans', 'Implementation Steps', 'Success Factors'];
---

<FrameworkLayout title="Blue Ocean Strategy" sections={sections}>
  <h1 id="overview">Blue Ocean Strategy</h1>
  
  <h2 id="overview">Overview</h2>
  <p>
    Blue Ocean Strategy, developed by W. Chan Kim and Renée Mauborgne, describes a market approach where companies create uncontested market spaces rather than competing in existing industries. Instead of fighting over shrinking profits in "red oceans" of intense competition, organizations can "swim in blue oceans" of untapped market potential.
  </p>

  <h2 id="core-principles">Core Principles</h2>
  
  <h3>Red Ocean vs. Blue Ocean</h3>
  <p>
    <strong>Red Ocean:</strong> Compete in existing industries with established rules. Competition for market share turns oceans "red" with competition.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Blue Ocean:</strong> Create new market spaces and new demand. Make competition irrelevant through differentiation and low cost.
  </p>

  <h3>Value Innovation</h3>
  <p>
    The core of blue ocean strategy is pursuing differentiation AND low cost simultaneously—not one or the other. This breaks the value-cost trade-off that defines red ocean competition.
  </p>

  <h2 id="creating-blue-oceans">Creating Blue Oceans</h2>
  <h3>The Four Actions Framework</h3>
  <ol>
    <li><strong>Eliminate:</strong> Remove factors the industry takes for granted</li>
    <li><strong>Reduce:</strong> Decrease factors below industry standards</li>
    <li><strong>Raise:</strong> Increase factors above industry standards</li>
    <li><strong>Create:</strong> Introduce factors the industry has never offered</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="implementation-steps">Implementation Steps</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Analyze the current competitive landscape (Strategy Canvas)</li>
    <li>Identify factors to eliminate, reduce, raise, and create</li>
    <li>Design the new value proposition</li>
    <li>Test and refine with potential customers</li>
    <li>Ensure profitability through smart execution</li>
    <li>Expand and defend the blue ocean space</li>
  </ol>

  <h2 id="success-factors">Success Factors</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Focus on the big picture, not just numbers</li>
    <li>Reach beyond existing customers to create new demand</li>
    <li>Get the strategic sequence right: utility → price → cost → adoption</li>
    <li>Overcome organizational hurdles through commitment and capability building</li>
    <li>Align the entire system toward the new strategy</li>
  </ul>
</FrameworkLayout>
